<div id="__nuxt"><div><main id="main-content" class="default-layout__main"><!--[--><div data-page="[uid].vue"><div class="outer-container"><div><!--[--><section id="equality-&amp;-diversity-policy" class="section-wrapper rich-text" index="0" data-v-92714c58 data-v-ebc71926><div class="section-wrapper__container" data-v-ebc71926><!--[--><!--[--><h1><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Equality &amp; Diversity Policy<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h1><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Scope<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->This policy applies to all Evri employees, casual workers, agency workers, recruitment applicants and contractors (collectively referred to as employees). It does not form part of any person&#39;s terms and conditions of employment and can at any time be reviewed and changed at the organisation’s discretion.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->This document supersedes all prior equality and diversity policies and procedures.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Purpose<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri is committed to promoting equality and diversity and promoting a culture that actively values difference and recognises that people from different backgrounds and experiences can bring valuable insights to the workplace and enhance the way we work. Evri aims to be an inclusive organisation, where diversity is valued, respected and built upon, with ability to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri is also committed to compliance with relevant equality legislation, including (but not limited to) the Equality Act 2010, Codes of Practice and relevant best practice guidance. This policy pursues and builds on the statutory position to ensure effective policies and practice of promoting equality. Evri aims to proactively tackle discrimination or disadvantage and aims to ensure that no individual or group is directly or indirectly discriminated against for any reason with regard to employment or accessing its services.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Definition of Equality and Diversity<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Equality can be described as breaking down barriers, eliminating discrimination and ensuring equal treatment, opportunity and access for all, which is supported and protected by legislation. Diversity can be described as celebrating differences and valuing everyone. Each person is an individual with visible and non-visible differences and by respecting this everyone can feel valued for their contributions which is beneficial not only for the individual but for Evri.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri is committed to ensuring that:<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><ul><!--[--><!--[--><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->People (including existing and former employees, job applicants, clients, customers, suppliers and visitors) are treated fairly and consistently in an environment which is free from any form of discrimination;<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->People (including existing and former employees, job applicants, clients, customers, suppliers and visitors) are protected from discrimination against the following characteristics as outlined in the Equality Act 2010: age; disability; gender reassignment; marriage or civil partnership status; pregnancy or maternity; race (includes colour, nationality and ethnic or national origins); religion or belief; sex and sexual orientation (the Protected Characteristics);<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->All employment-related policies, practices and procedures are applied impartially and objectively;<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Equality of opportunity to all and to provide employees with the opportunity to develop and realise their full potential;<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri works towards achieving a diverse workforce at all levels; and<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri&#39;s employees can work in an atmosphere of dignity and respect.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><!--]--><!--]--></ul><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->All Evri&#39;s employees will be treated fairly in an environment which is also free from any form of discrimination with regard to: caring responsibilities, part-time or fixed term employment, membership or non-membership of a trade union or spent convictions. <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri will not tolerate processes, attitudes and behaviour that amounts to unlawful discrimination. The following forms of discrimination are prohibited under this policy and are unlawful:<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><ol><!--[--><!--[--><li><!--[--><!--[--><strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Direct discrimination: <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->treating someone less favourably because of a protected characteristic.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Indirect discrimination: <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->a provision, criterion or practice that applies to everyone but adversely affects people with a particular protected characteristic more than others and is not justified.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Harassment: <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->this includes sexual harassment and other unwanted conduct related to a protected characteristic, which has the purpose or effect of violating someone&#39;s dignity or creating an intimidating, hostile, degrading, humiliating or offensive environment for them.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Victimisation: <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->retaliation against someone who has complained or has supported someone else&#39;s complaint about discrimination or harassment.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Disability discrimination: <!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></strong><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->this includes direct and indirect discrimination, any unjustified less favourable treatment because of the effects of a disability, and failure to make reasonable adjustments to alleviate disadvantages caused by a disability.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><!--]--><!--]--></ol><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Discrimination because someone associates with someone that has a protected characteristic is also prohibited.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri recognises the importance of monitoring, reviewing and reporting on its equality and diversity policy and practice and to measure progress in meeting our policy statement.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Practical support for a diverse workforce<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->As an employer committed to diversity and equality Evri recognises its success depends on creating a working environment which supports the diverse make-up of its employees with supporting policies and procedures to create a framework of balance.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Work/life balance<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->The company is committed to helping its employees fulfill their potential at work whilst finding the right work/life balance by offering flexible working hours and opportunities to job share where appropriate.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri has a framework of policies, such as Flexible Working, Additional Leave and Career Break policies, to help employees understand their options to ensure the correct work life balance.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Review and monitoring<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri undertakes monitoring that not only meets statutory requirements but also aims for best practice. This is used to inform and improve our employment practices. If, through monitoring, any discrimination is identified, the company will take corrective action to eliminate it.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Complaints<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri takes all complaints, including those relating to equality and diversity issues, very seriously and has a grievance and disciplinary policy in place to deal with such matters. Please refer to these policies for further details. If you believe that you have suffered discrimination you should raise the matter in accordance with our grievance procedure.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->People Strategy and Corporate Social Responsibility<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri aims to be an employer of choice and through its People Strategy aims to ensure its workforce can make a valuable contribution while ensuring we support our workforce’s health and well-being in the workplace.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Responsibilities<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->All employees have a responsibility to guard against any form of discrimination and avoid any action which goes against the terms or spirit of this policy. Therefore all employees must ensure that there is no discrimination in any of their decisions or behaviour. All employees must:<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><ul><!--[--><!--[--><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Report any suspected discriminatory acts, omissions, comments or practices;<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Not induce or attempt to induce others to practice unlawful discrimination;<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Co-operate with any measures introduced to ensure equality of opportunity;<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Not victimise anyone as a result of them having complained about, reported or provided evidence of discrimination: and<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Not harass, abuse or intimidate others.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><!--]--><!--]--></ul><h3><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->The Chief Executive and The Board are responsible for:<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h3><ul><!--[--><!--[--><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Providing leadership on the equality and diversity strategy and policy, acting as overall champions to ensure the policy is embedded within the business<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Communicating the strategy and policy, internally and externally<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Acting as ambassadors and exemplars of the strategy and policy<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><!--]--><!--]--></ul><h3><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Managers at all levels are responsible for:<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h3><ul><!--[--><!--[--><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Implementing the policy as part of their day-to day management of employees and in applying employment policies and practices in a fair and equitable way<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Ensuring equality and diversity issues are addressed in performance discussions<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Ensuring all employees act in accordance with the equality and diversity policy providing necessary support and direction<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Effectively managing and dealing promptly when investigating issues<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><!--]--><!--]--></ul><h3><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Each employee is responsible for:<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h3><ul><!--[--><!--[--><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Implementing the policy in their day-to-day work and their dealings with colleagues<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Ensuring their behaviour is appropriate to the policy and that they treat colleagues with respect and dignity<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Not discriminating against other employees<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Notifying their line manager of any concerns with regard to the conduct of other employees<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><!--]--><!--]--></ul><h3><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Human Resources are responsible for:<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h3><ul><!--[--><!--[--><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Developing employment policy and strategy on equality and diversity<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Providing guidance to line managers and employees<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Supporting managers in investigating issues relating to potential discrimination<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Monitoring employment policies and practices<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Championing the issues, internally and externally<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><li><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Facilitating training and development initiatives on equality and diversity, both at corporate and directorate level<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></li><!--]--><!--]--></ul><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Non-Compliance with policy<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Evri will not tolerate any behaviour that breaches our equality and diversity policy and any such breaches will be regarded as misconduct that will be dealt with in accordance with our disciplinary procedure. Serious breaches, such as unlawful discrimination, harassment or victimisation on grounds of a protected characteristic, may amount to gross misconduct and lead to dismissal from employment without notice.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Related Procedures and Processes<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->This policy should be read in conjunction with the Bullying &amp; Harassment policy, Disciplinary and Grievance policy and guidelines where appropriate.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Review<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->This document will be reviewed annually. If there are any changes prompted by legislation or case law, it will be reviewed to ensure compliance.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><h2><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Sign off and ownership<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></h2><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->This policy is owned by Human Resources.<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><p><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><!--v-if-->Updated May 2021<!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--></p><!--]--><!--]--></div></section><!--]--></div></div></div><!--]--></main></div></div><div id="teleports"></div><script>window.__NUXT__={};window.__NUXT__.config={public:{ENV_NAME:"prod",PUBLIC_PATH:"https://www.evri.com",WEB_BASE:"https://www.evri.com/",PRISMIC_REPO:"ev-mercury",DEVTOOLS:false,API_BASE:"https://api.hermesworld.co.uk/",AUTH0_USERS_ENDPOINT:"https://hermes-df-prod.eu.auth0.com/userinfo",AUTH0_CLIENT_ID:"dC8K22keYtRszHe7dnmlWSve2kP7mUBF",AUTH0_DOMAIN:"hermes-df-prod.eu.auth0.com",AUTH0_LOGIN_REDIRECT:"https://www.evri.com/",AUTH0_LOGOUT_REDIRECT:"https://www.evri.com/",ASSETLINKS_PATH:"assetlinks-prod.json",APPLE_MERCHANT_DOMAIN_PATH:"apple-developer-merchantid-domain-association-PROD.txt",APPLE_APP_SITE_ASSOCIATION_PATH:"apple-app-site-association-PROD",CHATBOT_URL:"https://chat-loader.smartagent.app/loader/main.js",FEATURE_SWITCH_URL:"https://www.evri.com/feature-switches/feature-switches.json",FINDER_URL:"https://location-finder.evri.com",BASKET_API_KEY:"4GuiGkQaE92687ICJtKNRd01hc4JBKUG",BULK_API_KEY:"WtuYb1yZMIGwLJzEm0yUzhLzPGuKS632",EVRI_API_KEY:"0DExZiK9in2ihGce7cDPrnpQ4s4nIpWG",HELP_API_KEY:"IfhFrxnv1JmbNW2tBA9hnRvG1o1vnsx2",SEND_API_KEY:"fHbmtsuSHrBH5gaC6m2QF9QG3YAycmgN",TRACK_NON_ROTATING_API_KEY:"MgMPMhWhXxSp7xIoYUVnWDklTl7EXAgG",GLOBAL_CSS_URI:"https://resources.hermescloud.co.uk/global/",ROUTER_BASE:"/",ACCOUNT_ENDPOINT:"https://api.hermesworld.co.uk/enterprise-user-account-api/v1/",BUSINESS_ACCOUNT_ENDPOINT:"https://api.hermesworld.co.uk/business-account-enquiry-api/v1/",CLIENTS_JSON:"https://www.evri.com/clients/clients.js",CUSTOMER_ORDER_ENDPOINT:"https://api.hermesworld.co.uk/customer-order-api/v1/",RETAILERS_ENDPOINT:"https://api.hermesworld.co.uk/enterprise-returns-api/v1/retailers",TRACKING_ENDPOINT:"https://tracking.platform-apis.evri.com/v1/",CUSTOMER_TRACKING_API:"https://api.evri.com/customer-tracking/v1/",GROOVY_PUBLISHER:"evri-tracking",WAF_SDK_URL:"https://d52c969eb9aa.edge.sdk.awswaf.com/d52c969eb9aa/3aa3b8a4ac7b/",ROTATING_API_KEYS_URL:"https://www.evri.com/protected/keys.json",OPENTEL_KEY:"MTU1Njg0ODpnbGNfZXlKdklqb2lNVFk1TnpNeU15SXNJbTRpT2lKbWNtOXVkR1Z1WkMxMGIydGxiaUlzSW1zaU9pSTJSVFJFZVRreGEyRk9kVVZVTnpFNWQycFBPSGsxTUZVaUxDSnRJanA3SW5JaU9pSndjbTlrTFdkaUxYTnZkWFJvTFRFaWZYMD0=","nuxt-scripts":{version:"",prefix:"/_scripts",defaultScriptOptions:{trigger:"onNuxtReady"},googleStaticMapsProxy:"",endpoints:{}},prismic:{endpoint:"https://ev-mercury.cdn.prismic.io/api/v2",environment:"",client:"~/prismic/client",linkResolver:"~/prismic/linkResolver",clientConfig:{routes:[{type:"home",path:"/"},{type:"amazon_mfn",path:"/amazonmfn"},{type:"business_page",path:"/business"},{type:"microshippers_price_groups",path:"/price-groups"},{type:"modal-page",path:"/modals/:uid"},{type:"pressHome",path:"/press"},{type:"press",path:"/press/:uid"},{type:"blogHome",path:"/news"},{type:"blog",path:"/news/:uid"},{type:"faq-page",path:"/faqs/:subpath2?/:uid",resolvers:{subpath2:"subpath2"}},{type:"landing-page",path:"/:uid"},{type:"content-page",path:"/:subpath1?/:subpath2?/:uid",resolvers:{subpath1:"subpath1",subpath2:"subpath2"}}]},preview:"/preview",toolbar:true,imports:["vue"],components:{richTextComponents:"~/prismic/richTextComponents"}}},app:{baseURL:"/",buildId:"513e9521-44ec-4b76-a82f-bb8aaa8e0497",buildAssetsDir:"/_nuxt/",cdnURL:""}}</script><script type="application/json" data-nuxt-data="nuxt-app" data-ssr="true" id="__NUXT_DATA__">[["ShallowReactive",1],{"prerenderedAt":2,"data":3,"state":263,"once":13571,"_errors":13572,"serverRendered":269,"path":13574,"pinia":13575},1784022582227,["ShallowReactive",4],{"content-page:equality-and-diversity-policy":5},{"uid":6,"document":7,"postSlices":262},"equality-and-diversity-policy",{"titleTag":8,"metaDescription":9,"canonical":10,"subpath1":11,"subpath2":13,"slices":14},"Equality & Diversity Policy | Evri","Evri is committed to promoting equality and diversity in our workplace. Read about how we approach this in our equality and diversity policy.","equality-and-diversity-policy.html\u002F\u002Fwww.evri.com\u002Fequality-and-diversity-policy",{"link_type":12},"Document",{"link_type":12},[15],{"variation":16,"version":17,"items":18,"primary":20,"id":259,"slice_type":260,"slice_label":261},"default-slice","sktwi1xtmkfgx8626",[19],{},{"content":21},[22,26,30,34,37,40,43,46,49,52,55,59,62,65,68,71,74,77,80,88,93,98,103,108,111,114,117,120,123,126,129,132,135,138,141,144,147,150,153,156,159,162,165,168,172,175,178,181,184,187,190,193,196,199,202,205,208,211,214,217,220,223,226,229,232,235,238,241,244,247,250,253,256],{"type":23,"text":24,"spans":25},"heading1","Equality & Diversity Policy",[],{"type":27,"text":28,"spans":29},"heading2","Scope",[],{"type":31,"text":32,"spans":33},"paragraph","This policy applies to all Evri employees, casual workers, agency workers, recruitment applicants and contractors (collectively referred to as employees). It does not form part of any person's terms and conditions of employment and can at any time be reviewed and changed at the organisation’s discretion.",[],{"type":31,"text":35,"spans":36},"This document supersedes all prior equality and diversity policies and procedures.",[],{"type":27,"text":38,"spans":39},"Purpose",[],{"type":31,"text":41,"spans":42},"Evri is committed to promoting equality and diversity and promoting a culture that actively values difference and recognises that people from different backgrounds and experiences can bring valuable insights to the workplace and enhance the way we work. Evri aims to be an inclusive organisation, where diversity is valued, respected and built upon, with ability to recruit and retain a diverse workforce.",[],{"type":31,"text":44,"spans":45},"Evri is also committed to compliance with relevant equality legislation, including (but not limited to) the Equality Act 2010, Codes of Practice and relevant best practice guidance. This policy pursues and builds on the statutory position to ensure effective policies and practice of promoting equality. Evri aims to proactively tackle discrimination or disadvantage and aims to ensure that no individual or group is directly or indirectly discriminated against for any reason with regard to employment or accessing its services.",[],{"type":27,"text":47,"spans":48},"Definition of Equality and Diversity",[],{"type":31,"text":50,"spans":51},"Equality can be described as breaking down barriers, eliminating discrimination and ensuring equal treatment, opportunity and access for all, which is supported and protected by legislation. Diversity can be described as celebrating differences and valuing everyone. Each person is an individual with visible and non-visible differences and by respecting this everyone can feel valued for their contributions which is beneficial not only for the individual but for Evri.",[],{"type":31,"text":53,"spans":54},"Evri is committed to ensuring that:",[],{"type":56,"text":57,"spans":58},"list-item","People (including existing and former employees, job applicants, clients, customers, suppliers and visitors) are treated fairly and consistently in an environment which is free from any form of discrimination;",[],{"type":56,"text":60,"spans":61},"People (including existing and former employees, job applicants, clients, customers, suppliers and visitors) are protected from discrimination against the following characteristics as outlined in the Equality Act 2010: age; disability; gender reassignment; marriage or civil partnership status; pregnancy or maternity; race (includes colour, nationality and ethnic or national origins); religion or belief; sex and sexual orientation (the Protected Characteristics);",[],{"type":56,"text":63,"spans":64},"All employment-related policies, practices and procedures are applied impartially and objectively;",[],{"type":56,"text":66,"spans":67},"Equality of opportunity to all and to provide employees with the opportunity to develop and realise their full potential;",[],{"type":56,"text":69,"spans":70},"Evri works towards achieving a diverse workforce at all levels; and",[],{"type":56,"text":72,"spans":73},"Evri's employees can work in an atmosphere of dignity and respect.",[],{"type":31,"text":75,"spans":76},"All Evri's employees will be treated fairly in an environment which is also free from any form of discrimination with regard to: caring responsibilities, part-time or fixed term employment, membership or non-membership of a trade union or spent convictions. ",[],{"type":31,"text":78,"spans":79},"Evri will not tolerate processes, attitudes and behaviour that amounts to unlawful discrimination. The following forms of discrimination are prohibited under this policy and are unlawful:",[],{"type":81,"text":82,"spans":83},"o-list-item","Direct discrimination: treating someone less favourably because of a protected characteristic.",[84],{"start":85,"end":86,"type":87},0,23,"strong",{"type":81,"text":89,"spans":90},"Indirect discrimination: a provision, criterion or practice that applies to everyone but adversely affects people with a particular protected characteristic more than others and is not justified.",[91],{"start":85,"end":92,"type":87},25,{"type":81,"text":94,"spans":95},"Harassment: this includes sexual harassment and other unwanted conduct related to a protected characteristic, which has the purpose or effect of violating someone's dignity or creating an intimidating, hostile, degrading, humiliating or offensive environment for them.",[96],{"start":85,"end":97,"type":87},12,{"type":81,"text":99,"spans":100},"Victimisation: retaliation against someone who has complained or has supported someone else's complaint about discrimination or harassment.",[101],{"start":85,"end":102,"type":87},15,{"type":81,"text":104,"spans":105},"Disability discrimination: this includes direct and indirect discrimination, any unjustified less favourable treatment because of the effects of a disability, and failure to make reasonable adjustments to alleviate disadvantages caused by a disability.",[106],{"start":85,"end":107,"type":87},27,{"type":31,"text":109,"spans":110},"Discrimination because someone associates with someone that has a protected characteristic is also prohibited.",[],{"type":31,"text":112,"spans":113},"Evri recognises the importance of monitoring, reviewing and reporting on its equality and diversity policy and practice and to measure progress in meeting our policy statement.",[],{"type":27,"text":115,"spans":116},"Practical support for a diverse workforce",[],{"type":31,"text":118,"spans":119},"As an employer committed to diversity and equality Evri recognises its success depends on creating a working environment which supports the diverse make-up of its employees with supporting policies and procedures to create a framework of balance.",[],{"type":27,"text":121,"spans":122},"Work\u002Flife balance",[],{"type":31,"text":124,"spans":125},"The company is committed to helping its employees fulfill their potential at work whilst finding the right work\u002Flife balance by offering flexible working hours and opportunities to job share where appropriate.",[],{"type":31,"text":127,"spans":128},"Evri has a framework of policies, such as Flexible Working, Additional Leave and Career Break policies, to help employees understand their options to ensure the correct work life balance.",[],{"type":27,"text":130,"spans":131},"Review and monitoring",[],{"type":31,"text":133,"spans":134},"Evri undertakes monitoring that not only meets statutory requirements but also aims for best practice. This is used to inform and improve our employment practices. If, through monitoring, any discrimination is identified, the company will take corrective action to eliminate it.",[],{"type":27,"text":136,"spans":137},"Complaints",[],{"type":31,"text":139,"spans":140},"Evri takes all complaints, including those relating to equality and diversity issues, very seriously and has a grievance and disciplinary policy in place to deal with such matters. Please refer to these policies for further details. If you believe that you have suffered discrimination you should raise the matter in accordance with our grievance procedure.",[],{"type":27,"text":142,"spans":143},"People Strategy and Corporate Social Responsibility",[],{"type":31,"text":145,"spans":146},"Evri aims to be an employer of choice and through its People Strategy aims to ensure its workforce can make a valuable contribution while ensuring we support our workforce’s health and well-being in the workplace.",[],{"type":27,"text":148,"spans":149},"Responsibilities",[],{"type":31,"text":151,"spans":152},"All employees have a responsibility to guard against any form of discrimination and avoid any action which goes against the terms or spirit of this policy. Therefore all employees must ensure that there is no discrimination in any of their decisions or behaviour. All employees must:",[],{"type":56,"text":154,"spans":155},"Report any suspected discriminatory acts, omissions, comments or practices;",[],{"type":56,"text":157,"spans":158},"Not induce or attempt to induce others to practice unlawful discrimination;",[],{"type":56,"text":160,"spans":161},"Co-operate with any measures introduced to ensure equality of opportunity;",[],{"type":56,"text":163,"spans":164},"Not victimise anyone as a result of them having complained about, reported or provided evidence of discrimination: and",[],{"type":56,"text":166,"spans":167},"Not harass, abuse or intimidate others.",[],{"type":169,"text":170,"spans":171},"heading3","The Chief Executive and The Board are responsible for:",[],{"type":56,"text":173,"spans":174},"Providing leadership on the equality and diversity strategy and policy, acting as overall champions to ensure the policy is embedded within the business",[],{"type":56,"text":176,"spans":177},"Communicating the strategy and policy, internally and externally",[],{"type":56,"text":179,"spans":180},"Acting as ambassadors and exemplars of the strategy and policy",[],{"type":169,"text":182,"spans":183},"Managers at all levels are responsible for:",[],{"type":56,"text":185,"spans":186},"Implementing the policy as part of their day-to day management of employees and in applying employment policies and practices in a fair and equitable way",[],{"type":56,"text":188,"spans":189},"Ensuring equality and diversity issues are addressed in performance discussions",[],{"type":56,"text":191,"spans":192},"Ensuring all employees act in accordance with the equality and diversity policy providing necessary support and direction",[],{"type":56,"text":194,"spans":195},"Effectively managing and dealing promptly when investigating issues",[],{"type":169,"text":197,"spans":198},"Each employee is responsible for:",[],{"type":56,"text":200,"spans":201},"Implementing the policy in their day-to-day work and their dealings with colleagues",[],{"type":56,"text":203,"spans":204},"Ensuring their behaviour is appropriate to the policy and that they treat colleagues with respect and dignity",[],{"type":56,"text":206,"spans":207},"Not discriminating against other employees",[],{"type":56,"text":209,"spans":210},"Notifying their line manager of any concerns with regard to the conduct of other employees",[],{"type":169,"text":212,"spans":213},"Human Resources are responsible for:",[],{"type":56,"text":215,"spans":216},"Developing employment policy and strategy on equality and diversity",[],{"type":56,"text":218,"spans":219},"Providing guidance to line managers and employees",[],{"type":56,"text":221,"spans":222},"Supporting managers in investigating issues relating to potential discrimination",[],{"type":56,"text":224,"spans":225},"Monitoring employment policies and practices",[],{"type":56,"text":227,"spans":228},"Championing the issues, internally and externally",[],{"type":56,"text":230,"spans":231},"Facilitating training and development initiatives on equality and diversity, both at corporate and directorate level",[],{"type":27,"text":233,"spans":234},"Non-Compliance with policy",[],{"type":31,"text":236,"spans":237},"Evri will not tolerate any behaviour that breaches our equality and diversity policy and any such breaches will be regarded as misconduct that will be dealt with in accordance with our disciplinary procedure. Serious breaches, such as unlawful discrimination, harassment or victimisation on grounds of a protected characteristic, may amount to gross misconduct and lead to dismissal from employment without notice.",[],{"type":27,"text":239,"spans":240},"Related Procedures and Processes",[],{"type":31,"text":242,"spans":243},"This policy should be read in conjunction with the Bullying & Harassment policy, Disciplinary and Grievance policy and guidelines where appropriate.",[],{"type":27,"text":245,"spans":246},"Review",[],{"type":31,"text":248,"spans":249},"This document will be reviewed annually. If there are any changes prompted by legislation or case law, it will be reviewed to ensure compliance.",[],{"type":27,"text":251,"spans":252},"Sign off and ownership",[],{"type":31,"text":254,"spans":255},"This policy is owned by Human Resources.",[],{"type":31,"text":257,"spans":258},"Updated May 2021",[],"rich_text$a1fdf1fb-8518-4979-a587-a6e592562f54","rich_text",null,[15],["Reactive",264],{"$sglobal-feature-switches":265,"$sclients":333,"$sglobal-basket-count":261},{"abtasty":266,"accessibe":270,"appPromoBanner":273,"autoDivertUpdates":277,"awin":280,"bulkInternational":283,"